{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/tests/smart_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.314236Z","id":"48391d8261943606f2c6ece411c2971b14b5eef4d75c57b75e1d55bf742715ee","body":{"detail":"jj() (crates/clax-git/tests/common.rs) looks at CLAX_TEST_JJ, then jj on PATH. Without either the test prints a skip line and passes. It ran with CLAX_TEST_JJ set to a jj 0.46.0 build: `CLAX_TEST_JJ=<path to jj> cargo test -p clax-git smart_http::jj` passes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":509},"end":{"line":513},"content_hash":"3b186b5e733e99a71260b8879b9319d0cb63ff3e597b2106449db84d2d4d7e49"},"summary":"The jj clone, fetch and push test passes without running when jj is not found","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
